    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "formulas_info",
      "content": "## Key Formulas\n\n**Density Formula:**\n- ρ = m / V\n  - ρ = density\n  - m = mass\n  - V = volume\n\n**Specific Weight Formula:**\n- γ = (m × g) / V = ρ × g\n  - γ = specific weight\n  - g = acceleration due to gravity (9.807 m/s² or 32.174 ft/s²)\n  - ρ = density\n\n**Example 1: Specific Weight of Water at 4°C (SI System)**\n- γ = 1000 kg/m³ × 9.807 m/s² = 9,807 N/m³ = 9.807 kN/m³\n\n**Example 2: Specific Weight of Water at 39°F (Imperial System)**\n- γ = 1.940 sl/ft³ × 32.174 ft/s² = 62.4 lbf/ft³\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- Maximum water density: 1000 kg/m³ at 4°C (39.2°F)\n- Temperature range for calculations: 0-370°C or 32-700°F\n- Valid pressure ranges: 0-100°C at 1 atm, >100°C at saturation pressure\n- Thermal expansion is non-linear with temperature"
